        "note_tweet": {
          "entities": {},
          "text": "I’ve stopped contributing to open source projects (not saying I’m not contributing anything, but it’s definitely not a full-time job anymore).\n\nOne of the main reasons is that AI is replacing my role. It makes me feel incredibly useless, and most of the time, open-source projects block you from using AI because most people care about code quality, styles, and design. For instance, Opus 4.6 can now do 80% of what I do. I’m now just a reviewer, and in the meantime, Opus 4.6’s max subscription is $200 per month. So, what about me?\n\nOn the other hand, open-source projects aren’t entirely bug-free. Now, I just copy-paste the open-source code into my codebase and let AI do hot-patching, and everything works. Ship things quickly is the only way to survive these days, but open-source projects will slow everything down.\n\nSo, I’m just doing something meaningful else, but definitely not open-source."
        },
